# Git already stores every text file in this repo with LF. Without this file,
# a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true writes them out as CRLF, and
# Prettier, whose endOfLine default is lf, then reports files as unformatted
# whose committed content is already correct. That gap was 39 files: Windows
# reported 96, Linux and CI would report 57.
#
# Normalising here makes the working tree match the blobs on every platform, so
# a formatting check means the same thing wherever it runs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit, so a misfire in Git's text detection can never rewrite a byte of
# these. Git already classifies them correctly; this only removes the question.
*.png binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ttf binary
